# actlog / PractiLog - repository-wide line-ending and binary policy.
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# The dev machine has core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites line endings on every
# checkout. With no attributes pinned, the same file comes back as LF or CRLF
# depending on who cloned it and when. That silently breaks two hard rules in
# AGENTS.md R2: PowerShell scripts must be CRLF, Dart sources must be LF.
# During the Task 57 commit (0a7e752) git printed ~75 "LF will be replaced by
# CRLF" warnings - every one of them was this missing policy showing up.
#
# Why adding this now is safe
# ---------------------------
# Measured 2026-11-22 against 413 tracked files: every text blob already stores
# LF in the index (i/lf), the only exceptions being 27 binaries (i/-text). The
# clean filter also normalises to LF, so declaring "text" here changes no blob
# and produces no re-normalisation diff. Only the checkout direction is pinned.
# Existing working-tree files are NOT rewritten by adding this file; the new
# eol= takes effect on the next checkout of each file.
#
# Rules
# -----
# 1. eol= is spelled out only where a project rule or a toolchain cares.
# 2. Windows-native build sources keep CRLF, matching the platform convention.
# 3. Binary types are declared explicitly so git never converts or diffs them.

# --- default: detect text, store LF in the index --------------------------
* text=auto

# --- must be LF (AGENTS.md R2 and cross-platform tooling) -----------------
*.dart        text eol=lf
*.sql         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.json        text eol=lf
*.toml        text eol=lf
*.lock        text eol=lf
*.md          text eol=lf
*.txt         text eol=lf
*.tsv         text eol=lf
*.csv         text eol=lf
*.py          text eol=lf
*.sh          text eol=lf
*.js          text eol=lf
*.mjs         text eol=lf
*.cjs         text eol=lf
*.ts          text eol=lf
*.css         text eol=lf
*.html        text eol=lf
*.xml         text eol=lf
*.svg         text eol=lf
*.cmake       text eol=lf
*.iss         text eol=lf
.gitignore    text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.metadata     text eol=lf
pubspec.yaml  text eol=lf
analysis_options.yaml text eol=lf

# --- must be CRLF (AGENTS.md R2: PowerShell scripts) ----------------------
*.ps1         text eol=crlf
*.psm1        text eol=crlf
*.psd1        text eol=crlf
*.bat         text eol=crlf
*.cmd         text eol=crlf

# --- Windows-native build sources: platform convention is CRLF ------------
*.cpp         text eol=crlf
*.cc          text eol=crlf
*.h           text eol=crlf
*.hpp         text eol=crlf
*.rc          text eol=crlf
*.manifest    text eol=crlf

# --- binary: never convert, never diff ------------------------------------
*.png         binary
*.jpg         binary
*.jpeg        binary
*.gif         binary
*.webp        binary
*.bmp         binary
*.ico         binary
*.psd         binary
*.ttf         binary
*.otf         binary
*.woff        binary
*.woff2       binary
*.zip         binary
*.7z          binary
*.gz          binary
*.xz          binary
*.exe         binary
*.dll         binary
*.pdb         binary
*.lib         binary
*.exp         binary
*.ilk         binary
*.obj         binary
*.so          binary
*.bin         binary
*.db          binary
*.sqlite      binary
*.sqlite3     binary
*.mp3         binary
*.wav         binary
*.mp4         binary
*.pdf         binary
